"id":"symbiote-supreme","name":"Symbiote Supreme"},{"id":"taskmaster","name":"Taskmaster"},{"id":"terrax","name":"Terrax"},{"id":"thanos","name":"Thanos"},{"id":"thanos-deathless","name":"Thanos (Deathless)"},{"id":"the-champion","name":"The Champion"},{"id":"the-destroyer","name":"The Destroyer"},{"id":"the-hood","name":"The Hood"},{"id":"the-leader","name":"The Leader"},{"id":"the-maker","name":"The Maker"},{"id":"the-overseer","name":"The Overseer"},{"id":"thing","name":"Thing"},{"id":"thor","name":"Thor"},{"id":"thor-jane-foster","name":"Thor (Jane Foster)"},{"id":"thor-ragnarok","name":"Thor (Ragnarok)"},{"id":"tigra","name":"Tigra"},{"id":"titania","name":"Titania"},{"id":"toad","name":"Toad"},{"id":"ultron","name":"Ultron"},{"id":"ultron-classic","name":"Ultron (Classic)"},{"id":"unstoppable-colossus","name":"Unstoppable Colossus"},{"id":"valkyrie","name":"Valkyrie"},{"id":"venom","name":"Venom"},{"id":"venom-the-duck","name":"Venom The Duck"},{"id":"venompool","name":"Venompool"},{"id":"vision","name":"Vision"},{"id":"vision-aarkus","name":"Vision (Aarkus)"},{"id":"vision-age-of-ultron","name":"Vision (Age of Ultron)"},{"id":"vision-deathless","name":"Vision (Deathless)"},{"id":"viv-vision","name":"Viv Vision"},{"id":"void","name":"Void"},{"id":"vox","name":"Vox"},{"id":"vulture","name":"Vulture"},{"id":"war-machine","name":"War Machine"},{"id":"wasp","name":"Wasp"},{"id":"wave","name":"Wave"},{"id":"werewolf-by-night","name":"Werewolf By Night"},{"id":"white-tiger","name":"White Tiger"},{"id":"wiccan","name":"Wiccan"},{"id":"winter-soldier","name":"Winter Soldier"},{"id":"wolverine","name":"Wolverine"},{"id":"wolverine-weapon-x","name":"Wolverine (Weapon X)"},{"id":"wolverine-x-23","name":"Wolverine (X 23)"},{"id":"wong","name":"Wong"},{"id":"yelena-belova","name":"Yelena Belova"},{"id":"yellow-jacket","name":"Yellow Jacket"},{"id":"yondu","name":"Yondu"},{"id":"summoned-symbioid","name":"Summoned Symbioid"},{"id":"ghost-rider-robbie-reyes","name":"Ghost Rider (Robbie Reyes)"}],"bosses":[{"id":"collector-act5","name":"The Collector","chapter":"5.2.6","summary":"Transfer Bane safely and take short damage openings as his health unlocks additional defenses. This is the Act 5 encounter, not the Abyss Collector."},{"id":"ultron-act5","name":"Ultron • Act 5","chapter":"5.4.6","summary":"Read the dormant buff before applying a debuff. Parry itself can activate the effect you are trying to avoid."},{"id":"crossbones-act6","name":"Crossbones • Act 6","chapter":"6.1.5","summary":"Prepare for opening Poison, Arc Overload regeneration, Bane and restricted power access. These mechanics are supported by March 2026 footage."},{"id":"sentinel-act6","name":"Sentinel","chapter":"6.1.6","summary":"March 2026 commentary supports Fisticuffs, Stun Immunity and a power-reset restriction. Prepare safe openings and avoid saving power through a reset."},{"id":"mister-sinister-act6","name":"Mister Sinister • Act 6","chapter":"6.2.2","summary":"Caustic Temper accepts Fury buffs and passive Furies. Cover Poison and keep Fury active; Dex-Fury supplies Fury buffs when you dex special-attack hits."},{"id":"champion-act6","name":"The Champion","chapter":"6.2.6","summary":"Provisional preparation: control Fury and Unstoppable, then follow the displayed final-phase dodge requirements. Earlier phase thresholds below are historical, not a verified October-2025 kit."},{"id":"medusa-act6","name":"Medusa • Act 6","chapter":"6.3.1","summary":"The retuned fight uses Bloody Mess: maintain a Bleed debuff or passive to remove the 90% damage reduction. Watch Auto-Block and avoid feeding Explosive Personality."},{"id":"captain-america-iw-act6","name":"Captain America (Infinity War)","chapter":"6.3.6","summary":"March 2026 commentary confirms the critical-hit gate, Destructive Feedback and the SP1 → SP2 → SP3 sequence. Prepare both a damage plan and a power-control or survival plan."},{"id":"grandmaster","name":"The Grandmaster","chapter":"6.4.6","summary":"Follow his rules to create Wounded damage windows. Prioritize prompts and special reactions over ordinary damage."},{"id":"gwenperion","name":"Gwenperion","chapter":"7.1.6","summary":"One of three alternative 7.1.6 bosses. Plan for repeated healing resets and power gain; the steps below are a recurring loop, not health phases."},{"id":"ice-phoenix","name":"Ice Phoenix","chapter":"7.1.6","summary":"One of three alternative 7.1.6 bosses. Handle opening Coldsnap, then coordinate your special timing with Encroaching Stun."},{"id":"spider-witch","name":"Spider-Witch","chapter":"7.1.6","summary":"One of three alternative 7.1.6 bosses. Manage Evade, critical-hit punishment and reversed controls during specials."},{"id":"gwenmaster","name":"Gwenmaster","chapter":"7.2.6","summary":"A six-objective fight, not six ordinary health phases: finish each Plot Armor challenge before its countdown ends to turn her next SP2 against her."},{"id":"kang-conqueror","name":"Kang the Conqueror","chapter":"7.3.6","summary":"Solve the Power Loop prompts to open Time Collapse damage windows. Before entering, check the linked path: some Paradox nodes impose separate conditions for dealing damage."},{"id":"superior-kang","name":"Superior Kang","chapter":"7.4.6","summary":"Four successive health bars, with different Wounded damage bonuses. Defeating each of the first three rewinds health and resets power, effects and Slipstream charges."},{"id":"scytalis","name":"Scytalis","chapter":"8.1.6","summary":"The winning decision changes with the health bar: bait the correct special, confirm the trap is armed, and choose a knockdown or Prowess-building finish."},{"id":"bahamet","name":"Bahamet","chapter":"8.2.6","summary":"Build his Volatility to produce a radiation wave; spend your special to earn Removal charges, then use the phase-specific method to weaken his armor."},{"id":"cerastes","name":"Cerastes","chapter":"8.3.6","summary":"Rotate three armor-breaking actions to create a damage window, then handle the changing lockout rules and final survival sequence."},{"id":"glykhan","name":"Glykhan","chapter":"8.4.6","summary":"Fight three successive health bars. Start damage chains by punishing a heavy or special, manage Divine Punishments, and survive the final Indestructible window."},{"id":"orochi","name":"Orochi (X-23)","chapter":"9.1.6","summary":"Six successive health bars. Stack damaging effects, then interrupt a heavy with your special during Violent Purge to create burst damage."},{"id":"lotan","name":"Lotan (Jane Foster)","chapter":"9.2.6","summary":"Five successive health bars. Each seal changes the required positioning and actions for removing Desecrated Charges; zero charges opens Sanctified damage time."},{"id":"dread-emperor-doom","name":"Dread Emperor Doom","chapter":"9.3.6","summary":"Remove Will through special-attack interactions rather than ordinary damage. Each depleted Will cycle advances the fight toward a heavy-attack finish."},{"id":"carina-chronoserpent","name":"Carina (Chronoserpent) — Overview","chapter":"9.4.6","summary":"Shared Act 9.4.6 mechanics and navigation for the three Carina variants: Mutant/Mystic Vulnerability with Encroaching ISO Infection, Science/Tech Vulnerability with Corrupted ISO Blast, and Skill/Cosmic Vulnerability with Corrupted ISO Traps."},{"id":"nameless-grandmaster","name":"Nameless Grandmaster","chapter":"Necropolis","summary":"The Necropolis finale adds stop signals, conditional instructions and changing controls. This is separate from the Act 6 Grandmaster."},{"id":"carina-mutant-mystic-vulnerability","name":"Carina — Mutant/Mystic Vulnerability","chapter":"9.4.6 · Fight A","summary":"Fight A of Act 9.4.6. The Signature Ability is Mutant-Mystic Vulnerability: Carina emulates Skill/Cosmic mechanics, while Mutant/Mystic attackers receive the intended class-pair advantages. The core route mechanic is Encroaching ISO Infection."},{"id":"carina-science-tech-vulnerability","name":"Carina — Science/Tech Vulnerability","chapter":"9.4.6 · Fight B","summary":"Fight B of Act 9.4.6. The Signature Ability is Science-Tech Vulnerability: Carina is treated as Mutant/Mystic in addition to Superior, while Science/Tech attackers receive the intended class-pair advantages. The core mechanic is Corrupted ISO Blast."},{"id":"carina-skill-cosmic-vulnerability","name":"Carina — Skill/Cosmic Vulnerability","chapter":"9.4.6 · Fight C","summary":"Fight C of Act 9.4.6. The Signature Ability is Skill-Cosmic Vulnerability: Carina emulates Science/Tech mechanics, while Skill/Cosmic attackers receive the intended class-pair advantages. Progress comes from Corrupted ISO Traps."},{"id":"chronoserpent-act10","name":"The Chronoserpent","chapter":"10.4.4","summary":"A 20-health-bar finale built around Vigor management, Major and Minor Modes, changing Special Attack timing, and a final knockout condition."}],"gameModes":[{"id":"battlegrounds","name":"Battlegrounds"},{"id":"alliance-war","name":"Alliance War"},{"id":"questing","name":"Questing"}]}